    "body": "Before: the texture gate refused 40 + 40 + 19 because it demanded exact closure. Legacy C:N and bases/CEC warnings (including a missing-Na = 0 default) ran alongside the newer cross-checks. Cross-check thresholds could be saved with nonsense values such as a negative tolerance. A method could in principle supply its own reporting unit, and a method's QUDT override relabelled SIS exports.\n\nAfter: these four YY-approved follow-ups are implemented in four commits, one per issue.\n\n- **#278 (8b68513e).** The blocking TEXTURE_CLOSURE gate uses `crossCheck.textureClosureTolerancePct` (default \u00b12, per lab) via policyService, inclusive. It reads stored numbers, units and censoring per replicate. Censored, non-numeric, non-% or ambiguous fractions are disclosed as NOT_EVALUATED and do not block. Texture derivation uses the same tolerance.\n- **#279 (e5b82a65).** The legacy matrix C:N and bases/CEC advisories are retired. The crossChecks are the only advisory source, and Na is never assumed to be 0. `matrixDiagnostics` discloses `retiredAdvisories` and `advisorySuccessor`. One consequence for reviewers: a sample whose lab is not registered now sees no C:N advisory at all, only the disclosed `CROSS_CHECK_LAB_REQUIRED`.\n- **#281 (76ff9dd9).** Registry bounds are added: texture tolerance 0\u2013100, base saturation \u2265 0, C:N min and max \u2265 0, carbonate pH 0\u201314, bases/CEC factor \u2265 1. Defaults are unchanged and an out-of-range save is refused with POLICY_VALUE_INVALID. A value stored before the bounds existed is never rewritten:\n  - It resolves as invalid only for these keys, so the lab's other policies keep working.\n  - Save and submit return `CROSS_CHECK_POLICY_INVALID`, with no evidence rows written. This is localized in five locales.\n  - Texture derivation and the blocking gate fall back to exact closure, never a wider tolerance. **Audit please confirm this choice.**\n  - The policy page flags the stored value.\n- **#283 (5ca14d07).** One unit per analysis. The dead `ctx.method?.unit` fallback is removed. Both SIS exports label values with the analysis QUDT unit only. A disagreeing method override is ignored and disclosed as `unitDiagnostic: METHOD_UNIT_OVERRIDE_IGNORED`, which is declared in the V2 capabilities. There is no conversion and no stored-unit rewrite.\n\n**How.**\n- No migration and no data rewrite. Policy goes through policyService and the registry only.\n- New contract tests: `issue_278_texture_closure_policy` (18), `issue_281_cross_check_bounds` (17) and `issue_283_one_unit_per_analysis` (4). The historical matrix and cross-check evidence tests are rewritten as retirement tests for #279.\n- Local results:\n  - **Full server suite on #278\u2013#281:** 5150/5158 passed. Of the 8 failures, 6 come from this sandbox: there is no Playwright browser and no client build in that worktree. The other 2 are a load timeout in `audit_4_8_cross_check_evidence`, which passes 19/19 when run alone.\n  - **#283 on its own:** it was not in that full run. Its own tests and the 10 SIS and unit-related suites pass (140 tests).\n  - **Client:** on the final head, the client build passes and lint shows 0 errors.\n- Follow-up noted, not in this PR: the PDF metrology box and interpretationService still recompute texture at exact closure.\n\n**Merge hold:** this must not merge until the ae64f169 release is live.\n\nRefs #278, #279, #281, #283\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01869phMNBbSrZkcCR7UBe9J",
